            "text": "And what are the things that make one an ascetic and a brahmin? You should train like this: 'We will have conscience and prudence.' Now, mendicants, you might think, 'We have conscience and prudence. This is sufficient; enough has been done. We have achieved the goal of life as an ascetic. There is nothing more to do.' And you might rest content with just that much. I declare this to you, mendicants, I announce this to you: 'You who seek to be true ascetics, do not lose sight of the goal of the ascetic life while there is still more to do.'"
