        "inference": "The argument is about control and ownership, not existence. Notice that the text never says 'there is no person'; it says nothing you can point to behaves like a self you own. The interrogation adds a separate premise — impermanence — and the conclusion is practical: disenchantment. Read it as a diagnosis of grasping, not a metaphysical denial.",
