        "oneIdea": "Terms come in clusters, and the distinctions inside a cluster are doctrinal work.",
        "context": "Translators render clusters of Pali terms with overlapping English words, and the overlaps hide distinctions the texts rely on. Sati and sampajañña both become 'mindfulness' or 'awareness'; vitakka and vicāra both become 'thought'; saṅkhāra becomes 'formations', 'choices', or 'volitional activities' depending on the translator. This session maps three clusters using the glossary and the passages, without making new philological claims.",
